<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore to host regional telecom regulators' meet.</title>
<headline>Singapore to host regional telecom regulators' meet.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Telecommunication Authority of Singapore (TAS) said on Monday it would host the third meeting of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations Telecommunication Regulators' Council (ATRC).</p>
<p>The agenda would include discussions on the international rate settlement system, harmonising standards and broadband interconnectivity in ASEAN, TAS said in a statement.</p>
<p>The meeting is scheduled to take place from August 6 through August 8.</p>
<p>Delegates would include industry and regulatory representatives from ASEAN nations and members of the International Telecommunication Union (ITU), TAS said.</p>
<p>Singapore currently holds the annually rotating chairmanship of the ATRC. Previous chairing nations were Indonesia and Malaysia.</p>
</text>
